//! Synthetic local CA/server certificate fixtures for the Slice1 `DoT` tests.
//!
//! Every certificate and key here is synthetic, non-secret, and was generated
//! solely for these tests. No real service certificate or private key is
//! checked in, and nothing in this module is compiled into the library.
//!
//! ## Provenance
//!
//! Generated with OpenSSL 3.6.4 (Homebrew, `/opt/homebrew/bin/openssl`) on
//! 2026-09-16 using a throwaway directory outside the repository; only the DER
//! bytes below were copied in. The two roots are self-signed EC P-256
//! authorities with `basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE` and
//! `keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign`:
//!
//! ```text
//! openssl ecparam -name prime256v1 -genkey -noout -out ca.key.pem
//! openssl req -x509 -new -key ca.key.pem -out ca.pem -sha256 \
//!   -not_before 20240101000000Z -not_after 20360101000000Z \
//!   -subj "/CN=mosdns-slice1-synthetic-root-a" \
//!   -addext "basicConstraints=critical,CA:TRUE" \
//!   -addext "keyUsage=critical,keyCertSign,cRLSign"
//! ```
//!
//! Each leaf is an EC P-256 key signed by one of those roots with
//! `basicConstraints=critical,CA:FALSE`, `keyUsage=critical,digitalSignature`,
//! `extendedKeyUsage=serverAuth`, and a `subjectAltName=DNS:<name>`:
//!
//! ```text
//! openssl req -new -key leaf.key.pem -out leaf.csr -subj "/CN=<name>"
//! openssl x509 -req -in leaf.csr -CA ca.pem -CAkey ca.key.pem -set_serial N \
//!   -sha256 -not_before <nb> -not_after <na> -extfile leaf.ext -out leaf.crt
//! ```
//!
//! | Fixture | Subject / SAN | Issuer | Validity (UTC) |
//! | --- | --- | --- | --- |
//! | `LEAF_GOOD_A` | `dns.example` | root A (trusted) | 2024-01-01 – 2036-01-01 |
//! | `LEAF_WRONG_NAME_A` | `other.example` | root A (trusted) | 2024-01-01 – 2036-01-01 |
//! | `LEAF_EXPIRED_A` | `dns.example` | root A (trusted) | 2020-01-01 – 2021-01-01 |
//! | `LEAF_UNKNOWN_ISSUER_B` | `dns.example` | root B (untrusted) | 2024-01-01 – 2036-01-01 |
//!
//! Root A is the only anchor in `root_store_a()`; root B is deliberately never
//! added, which is what makes `LEAF_UNKNOWN_ISSUER_B` an unknown-issuer case.
//! `LEAF_EXPIRED_A` is expired relative to any realistic test run, so the
//! expiry case needs no clock control. The remaining cases are hostname
//! mismatch and untrusted issuer, neither of which depends on wall-clock time.

#![allow(dead_code)]

